id: pm-kb5h
title: "Source-tree folder-density program: bounded directory fan-out via domain-noun subfolders (zero feature loss)"
description: "Inter-file half of the 2026-07-12 too-many/too-long directive (intra-file LOC half = pm-yh8r): regroup high-fan-out directories (src/cli/commands 72, tests/unit/commands 60, tests/integration 32, scripts 23, src/cli 19) into domain-noun subfolders per the disposition blueprint in the body, in 6 fenced tranches."
type: Chore
status: open
priority: 1
tags[2]: "area:quality",refactor
created_at: "2026-07-12T19:14:42.057Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-04T09:18:07.504Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 600
acceptance_criteria: Every tracked source directory holds ≤~20 direct files or carries a documented exemption in this body; all moves land as import-specifier-only refactors with full gates green per tranche and byte-identical CLI/MCP/contract surface; pm files links updated for moved paths on open items in the same tranche; vitest/eslint-suppressions/coverage/package.json/workflow/docs references updated within the moving tranche
parent: pm-92if
risk: medium
confidence: 75
dependencies[2]{id,kind,created_at}:
